Usage:
```
mkdir build
cd build
cmake ..
make
./src/CocosTest
```

Standalone frame pacing tests (no graphics device or JavaScript engine):
```
cmake -S native/tests/unit-test -B native/tests/unit-test/build-frame-pacer -DCC_FRAME_PACER_TESTS_ONLY=ON
cmake --build native/tests/unit-test/build-frame-pacer --config Debug --target frame_pacer_tests
ctest --test-dir native/tests/unit-test/build-frame-pacer -C Debug --output-on-failure
```
Run these commands from the repository root. On Windows, select an installed
Visual Studio generator and architecture when configuring, for example
`-G "Visual Studio 17 2022" -A x64`. The tests use an injected clock/waiter and do
not sleep. They are also included in the normal CocosTest target.

The Android Engine integration is experimental: enable it with
`-DUSE_ANDROID_FRAME_PACER=ON` in the Android application's CMake configuration.
It defaults to OFF; XR builds and non-Android platforms retain the legacy path.
